{
  "summary": "Fixed a bug where parseInt was using radix 3 instead of 10, causing incorrect session limit parsing. This was likely an accidental typo that would cause maxSessionsPerType to have wrong values.",
  "learnings": [
    {
      "topic": "parseInt usage",
      "reminder": "Always use radix 10 with parseInt unless specifically parsing in another base. Common typo: 'parseInt(x, 10)' not 'parseInt(x, 3)'"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Environment variable parsing",
      "reminder": "When parsing numeric env vars with parseInt, always specify radix 10 explicitly to avoid silent bugs"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Code review checklist",
      "reminder": "Verify all numeric literals in function calls are intentional, especially radix parameters"
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "type": "bug",
      "description": "parseInt used radix 3 instead of 10 - would parse '10' as '3', causing session limits to be severely underestimated",
      "line": 24,
      "fix": "Changed from parseInt(..., 3) to parseInt(..., 10)"
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    "Consider extracting this parsing logic to a helper function to make it more testable",
    "Add validation that maxSessionsPerType is within reasonable bounds after parsing",
    "The fallback '3' in the env var default suggests 3 sessions - this could be documented or made configurable"
  ],
  "praise": "Bug was caught and fixed. The fix is minimal and surgical - only changes what needs to change.",
  "overallScore": 95,
  "codeQualityScore": 90,
  "testCoverageScore": 85,
  "documentationScore": 80
}

